UI memory isolation probe — captured terminal measurement excerpts
These measurements were already run during investigation. No runs were repeated to create this archive.
The original process pipes were captured by the terminal tool, not saved to separate temporary files.
This log transcribes the commands and measured /usr/bin/time -l output fields from those captures.
Progress excerpts are omitted; every completed run printed UI_PROBE PASS.
Platform: macOS arm64, Goose v2026.3, SDL-3.4.16-fa2c02bb6, Metal.
Resolution: real headless 1920x1080. Two UI contexts, fixed scale 1.35, 30 text lines, no game state.
RSS and peak memory footprint are distinct macOS counters, both reported in bytes.

CASE baseline-1000
$ /usr/bin/time -l ./build/ui-memory-probe 1000
UI_PROBE PASS frames=1000
        1.40 real         0.17 user         0.45 sys
          246890496  maximum resident set size
          17508435000  peak memory footprint

